  <h1>About</h1>
  <p class="lede">Tech lead at Apollo, in Delhi. Eight years of backend work. Messaging at Snapdeal first. Email, sequences, and agents now.</p>

  <h2>What I do</h2>
  <p>Apollo is sales engagement. I work on deliverability and sequences, and on the agent layer next to them. I was on the small team that shipped the Claude connector and MCP server in about ten days. From Claude you can search people, enrich them, and add them to a sequence.</p>
  <p>Before that, Snapdeal. Notifications and WhatsApp. The bugs that stuck were off the happy path. Counts that drifted. One slow Aerospike shard, then retries that took the system with them. A bot setup that had turned into a pile of special cases.</p>
  <p>On the side I'm building <a href="https://tomsdiary.ink" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">a diary</a> that writes back. The half-finished thoughts about agents and repos are on <a href="https://x.com/theybanjan" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">X</a>.</p>

  <h2>How I work</h2>
  <p>I care more about the second run than the demo. What happens twice, late, or halfway through a failure. Small steps you can undo. Notes the next person can use.</p>

  <h2>Stack</h2>
  <p>Ruby, Go, Java, Python. PostgreSQL, MongoDB, Redis, Aerospike, Kafka, Kubernetes. Prometheus, Grafana, Datadog, OpenTelemetry. Lately Claude, Cursor, and whatever gateway is in front of the model.</p>
